# Principal type violation: Any acts as both top and bottom of the type lattice.
# $f has type Fn(Any -> Any) because x is unannotated. Calling $f returns Any.
# The type system infers result: Any, which is a subtype of every concrete type.
# This means the type checker cannot distinguish well-typed from ill-typed code
# when Any flows through -- it accepts everything, losing the Damas-Milner
# principal type guarantee (doc/06 Limitation #2).
# At eval time, $f is the identity function, so the result is "hello" (a string).
[f: [fn [x] x]
 result: [f "hello"]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x), "result": String("hello")})
